A handler logs `Error [ERR_HTTP_HEADERS_SENT]: Cannot set headers after they are sent to the client`. What is the most likely cause?

```js
http.createServer((req, res) => {
  res.end('ok');
  res.setHeader('X-Trace', id);
});
```

Requests to this route never complete; the browser spinner keeps going until it times out. Why?

```js
http.createServer((req, res) => {
  res.writeHead(200, { 'Content-Type': 'text/plain' });
  res.write('hello');
});
```

In this Express 5 app, `req.body` is `undefined` inside the route even though the client sends valid JSON with `Content-Type: application/json`. Why?

```js
app.post('/orders', (req, res) => {
  res.json({ received: req.body });
});
app.use(express.json());
```

An Express app has this error handler at the end of the stack, but errors still produce Express's default HTML error page. Why?

```js
app.use((err, req, res) => {
  res.status(500).json({ error: err.message });
});
```

A TCP client sends two JSON messages with two separate `write` calls. The server parses each `data` event with `JSON.parse` and sometimes crashes with `Unexpected token {`. Why?

```js
socket.write('{"a":1}');
socket.write('{"b":2}');
// server
sock.on('data', (d) => handle(JSON.parse(d)));
```

A plain `node:http` handler tries to send JSON like this. What happens?

```js
http.createServer((req, res) => {
  res.setHeader('Content-Type', 'application/json');
  res.end({ ok: true });
});
```

Large uploads to a JSON endpoint return `500` instead of `413 Payload Too Large`. The app uses `express.json()` and this error handler. What is wrong?

```js
app.use((err, req, res, next) => {
  res.status(500).json({ error: err.message });
});
```

What status code does the client receive, and what does the server log?

```js
http.createServer((req, res) => {
  res.write('partial ');
  try {
    res.writeHead(500);
  } catch (e) {
    console.log(e.code);
  }
  res.end('done');
});
```

A health checker calls 200 internal URLs every few seconds and only reads `res.ok`, never the body:

```js
const res = await fetch(url);
return res.ok;
```

Over hours, connection counts to the targets climb and memory grows, although no errors are thrown. What is the fix?

A streaming CSV export route fails halfway because the database cursor errors. The app's error handler runs, then crashes with `ERR_HTTP_HEADERS_SENT`. What should the handler do?

```js
app.use((err, req, res, next) => {
  res.status(500).json({ error: 'Export failed' });
});
```

In Fastify 5, a plugin adds a decorator, but routes registered next to it fail with `fastify.db is undefined`:

```js
async function dbPlugin(fastify) {
  fastify.decorate('db', createPool());
}
fastify.register(dbPlugin);
fastify.register(async (app) => {
  app.get('/users', () => app.db.query('select 1'));
});
```

Why?
